menu "Postern"

    comment "GPIOs are on the chip that runs this component. -1 means unset."
    comment "Defaults are the M5Stamp Pico reference wiring. GPIO26 is reserved and is not a symbol. GPIO1 and GPIO3 stay UART0."
    comment "This image sets Classic Bluetooth A2DP, the external codec, AAC, and two stream endpoints in sdkconfig.defaults. A project that reuses the component sets the same symbols."

    config POSTERN_I2S_BCLK_GPIO
        int "I2S bit clock GPIO"
        range -1 48
        default 18
        help
            Input. The peer is the I2S master and drives this clock.
            The Stamp Pico reference uses GPIO18.

    config POSTERN_I2S_WS_GPIO
        int "I2S word-select GPIO"
        range -1 48
        default 19
        help
            Input. Word select, also called LRCK.
            The Stamp Pico reference uses GPIO19.

    config POSTERN_I2S_DIN_GPIO
        int "I2S data-in GPIO"
        range -1 48
        default 36
        help
            Input. PCM arrives on this pin. This component does not send audio back.
            The Stamp Pico reference uses GPIO36, which is input-only.

    config POSTERN_I2C_SDA_GPIO
        int "I2C SDA GPIO"
        range -1 48
        default 21
        help
            This chip is the I2C peripheral.
            The Stamp Pico reference uses GPIO21.

    config POSTERN_I2C_SCL_GPIO
        int "I2C SCL GPIO"
        range -1 48
        default 22
        help
            The Stamp Pico reference uses GPIO22.

    config POSTERN_I2C_ADDRESS
        hex "I2C peripheral address"
        range 0x00 0x7f
        default 0x1D
        help
            7-bit address. The Stamp Pico reference uses 0x1D.
            0x00 means this build has not chosen one.

endmenu
